{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/79695-my-probelm-with-changeling","id":79695,"title":"My Probelm with Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-25T15:28:35-08:00","id":79695,"title":"My Probelm with Changeling","content":"I know that there's a C20 thread right now that's gone off tangent a bit towards this, but I felt that I'd rather start a new thread instead of risking derailing that one further.<br /> <br /> With M20 around the corner and Wr20 in the works, to some extent talk of C20 is a bit early. However, as has been noted elsewhere, CtD has always teetered a bit on the edge of whether or not it is popular enough to really sell and if we're going to see C20 drumming up support for it is important.<br /> <br /> My problem though, is that I really don't like CtD as is. I think it has a lot of potential as a game, but to fix it enough that I'd really want to buy it I would need one core issue addressed that goes beyond cleaning up rules, fixing some of the fluff, or promises to avoid artwork that completely fails to sell the game's potential.<br /> <br /> I think my position is best summed up simply as: Changeling: the Dreaming lacks nuance to the point where it actively harms the theme of the game.<br /> <br /> Having a game about the loss of creativity, imagination, and so on in the world is a good start. But the game shoots itself in the foot by being extremely heavy-handed and binary about the concepts of what &quot;wonder&quot; is, and what the central struggle of the game is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> The game presents lots of interesting places to take things. For example it presents the concept of Court as being mutable with shifts between Seelie and Unseelie some thing that occurs for many changelings. But it never discusses it in any real detail (and then starts throwing in groups that are always one or the other anyway). There's no incentive in the games to have your character explore both sides of themselves. There's no conflict between these two aspects of their personality.<br /> <br /> Banality is a neat concept, but the game avoids a nuanced approach to what counts as Banal for borderline insulting generalizations (aging = banal, science/tech = banal, social norms = banal or art = not banal, liberal arts colleges = not banal, deviant behavior = not banal). Sure the game tries to walk this back a bit (if a scientific achievement captures the public imagination in can cause an explosion of glamour... but what about the simple events like a group of scientists discovering a brand new species?), but never really takes the steps to codify this as something that matters to play.<br /> <br /> Even the artwork, which most people seem to agree does a poor service to the game, is really problematic because of it being very one-sided. Typing this reminds me of an episode of the SyFy show Face Off where the contestants had to design &quot;Burton-esque&quot; (which I believe is the title of the episode) costumes. They had to capture something both whimsical and fantastic, with something dark and twisted. One of the top designs was a Cellist. It's a beautiful piece. But what twists it into also being dark is that her cello is also her lover... and if she doesn't play often enough he dies. It is touchingly sweet and disturbingly tragic at the same time. Something CtD's artwork and fluff often seems to fail to find the right balance for. It isn't that a balloon carrying talking bear can't be part of the artwork, but it needs a twist. Even something as simple as the balloons having faces; they show fear if the bear offers them to another, or start to silently scream and cry if they're released. We don't even need to know why. It just adds the edge of something not being 100% right with the situation and lets us see a hidden darkness behind the bubbly art.<br /> <br /> My biggest concern with getting interested in C20 is, well, that none of this is going to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 02-25-2014, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T15:39:18-08:00","id":79704,"title":"","content":"Very well said. That captures a lot of the problems I hope they would fix if they do a C20. Though I would also add the problem (as I stated in the other Changeling thread) that in general the story suffers because it is too easy to run away from your problems and the consequences of your actions, and what is more, this is not only made an option by the system, it's actually encouraged. It is a bitch and a half to tell a cohesive story when at every bump in the road or sign of conflict, the characters can run off to the land of make-believe to escape it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T16:15:28-08:00","id":79726,"title":"","content":"I couldn't agree more. I bought most of the 2nd Ed books (having been seduced by the artwork), but could never really get into the setting for most of the reasons you outlined.<br /> <br /> I hope that C20 happens, and pleases it's fans, but I have found &quot;The Lost&quot; to be far closer to what I had wanted from the fae genre.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T17:15:00-08:00","id":79774,"title":"","content":"I think there's room for Dreaming and Lost to coexist. They focus on very different things in the same genre. I enjoy Lost immensely because it is a very solid game. But I don't think Dreaming needs to be Lost. There are only some specific things I think Dreaming would benefit from taking from Lost (much more flexible character generation instead of the very rigid Dreaming Kiths being the big one for me).<br /> <br /> I want to see C20 be Dreaming; not something else. I just want it to break the pattern of V20 and W20 (and probably M20 but we haven't seen it yet) of not addressing some of the deeper issues with those games in the name of being true to the games as befits an anniversary edition. It should absolutely have everything in it that makes its fans love it so much. But there's so much room to make Dreaming the game it always could have been that would sell to all the people that could never get past some of the frustrating elements of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T17:47:11-08:00","id":79784,"title":"","content":"I will agree that there is room for both Dreaming and Lost. Let's also not forget Dark Ages Fae, which I personally believe to be BY FAR the superior White Wolf Fae game line. All three are very different games though and should each be judged on their own merits and weaknesses.<br /> <br /> The difference between C20 and V20 or W20 is that Vampire and Werewolf were successful lines up until the end. Changeling, whatever anyone may think of it, collapsed. It just wasn't popular enough. That means that when making a new edition it's not good enough to just rehash the old stuff the fans loved and repackage it with some setting and rules updates. It won't sell. It didn't sell then and it won't now. If they want C20 to be successful, as I do, I think they really need to take a harder look at why it failed in the first place and address some core issues with the game itself. Vampire and Werewolf and (hopefully) Mage are anniversary editions appealing to all the many people who loved them in the old days. Changeling needs to be more if it is going to stand up on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:05:08-08:00","id":80360,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>There's nothing wrong here now (thank you!), but I want to remind people not to </b><b>venture into edition waring, and to remain respectful to both the material they are critiquing and its fans.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:32:56-08:00","id":80392,"title":"","content":"Hmm.I've not read Changeling: The Lost, so I can't comment on it, but when I originally came across an ad for Changeling: The Dreaming (It had a street sign pointing to Nania and a dragon peering around a corner) I was very impressed with the feeling of wonder that that the line seemed to have. Years later, I'm not so sure it is a good match for a WoD game. Although I still appreciate the concept. Now, after reading The Dresden Files, I find myself thinking that this might be the type of Fae that I might want to put in my CWoD games. Not decided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T12:47:52-08:00","id":80438,"title":"","content":"Lost and Dreaming are, terminology aside, two of the more different games between WoDs, along with Mummy. I really enjoy them both.<br /> <br /> Dreaming always did have some odd variation on what constituted Banality. My thought is have C20 give some general suggestions but avoid nailing it down too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:15:11-08:00","id":80454,"title":"","content":"I think on the topic of describing Banality, it would be good to take the route that the Mage games have regarding vulgar vs. not vulgar magic. Give examples of superficially similar situations where one is Banal and the other is not. For example:<br /> <br /> Flipping burgers at O'Tolley's is dreary mind-numbing work and is Banal. Being a chef in a craft burger joint lets you be creative and artistic and is not Banal.<br /> <br /> What you're doing in both situations is effectively the same: making burgers. The technology and the materials aren't the key difference. The difference is that one is cookie-cutter and designed for uniformity, while the other is designed to be unique and experimental.<br /> <br /> I feel that using a few examples like that help get the point of Banality across and avoid some of the sillier over-generalizations of the original books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:25:06-08:00","id":80462,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms, I like your thinking on banality. To take a couple of classic Changeling stereotypes:<br /> <br /> Being an accountant who goes to work, does nothing but crunch numbers all day, and then goes home is banal. Being an accountant who gets creative with numbers, finds solutions to a company's problems in the numbers, and furthers their goals with the numbers is not banal.<br /> <br /> Being a librarian whose main concern is that all the books are in their place and no one speaks above a whisper is banal. Being a librarian who introduces kids to whole new worlds through books and makes in their mission to find everyone the book that speaks to them is not banal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:23:23-08:00","id":80501,"title":"","content":"I always looked at Changeling as trying desperately to hold onto magic and wonder as it is cruelly ripped away from you. These are people who are part of the magical world, both beautiful and terrifying. The world around them naturally poisons them, stripping away a reality they can only share with a small number of people. You go on adventures partly because something needs doing, but also because it is part of what you are. <br /> <br /> I'm a main-game Wraith guy myself, but Changeling was something I could sink my teeth into as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T00:40:29-08:00","id":80866,"title":"","content":"I loved the premise of Changeling the Dreaming. Each of the original games was a vehicle to explore critical philosophical dilemmas of humanity, and the question of Changeling was: How does one balance the needs of the child within against the demands of the world without? To that end, I never concerned myself with the artwork, or the pseudo-descriptive terms for banality and glamour. What was most distressing was the inability to see the congruence of meaning above the limitations of preconception. Inspired science is as glamorous as inspired jazz. Equally, uninspired science is as banal as Leonard Nemoy singing &quot;Sitting on the dock of the bay&quot;. (If you have ever heard the LP, you know what I mean, and if you haven't - protect your soul and don't.)<br /> <br /> Where Changeling the Dreaming was impossible for me was the actual mechanics of the powers. The total 'if-iness' of whether or not the cards would combine to permit a bunk within the purview of the PC left me unwilling to play the game. However, I still love the setting, the factions, and kithain. In my private outline, I have place for a population of 300 Nunehi and traditional Kithain. However, because of the radically different mechanics I have no intention of making them a functional part of any action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T01:30:03-08:00","id":80901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/79695-my-probelm-with-changeling?p=80866#post80866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one balance the needs of the child within against the demands of the world without?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me though, this is part of my problem with it. Imagination and wonder aren't limited to children. Neverland vs. Cubical farm doesn't make for an critical philosophical dilemma, because as I started this thread, it is so lacking in nuance you never really get anywhere with it.<br /> <br /> Childhood is awesome and growing up sucks is just as conflict killing as music is awesome and science sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T02:08:57-08:00","id":80922,"title":"","content":"I want three things out of a Changeling 20:<br /> <br /> 1) Make something the people who love it will adore<br /> 2) Make it better so it will draw in others as well<br /> 3) Make something I can use as antagonists or allies in my Werewolf games, because as is I never saw how Changelings fit as the fae that were referenced.<br /> <br /> Easy peasy right?<br /> <br /> I never really got into the game, bought the first edition rule book, but nothing else, but would love to in the future. I\u2019d buy a PoD copy of Changeling 20 at least. (Planning the same with Wraith, having never gotten into that game either). But man, one of my favorite \u201cgenres\u201d is kids with superpowers and it seems like Changeling could be close enough to that to be something I might enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T18:19:16-08:00","id":81348,"title":"","content":"V20 was written as a &quot;love letter to and in honor of the fans of V:tM&quot; (paraphrased.) Other than update the book so that the material wasn't stuck in 1999 (updating technology and getting rid of costs of living, etc.), making some rules tweaks, and including mechanics/splats for everything they could find, V20 didn't really introduce new concepts to the game. That was done purposefully, and it shows. Even the supplements (so far) haven't really upset the understanding/concept of the game.<br /> <br /> W20 was very similar, taking the expected and understood stuff that fans knew, updating it, and including as much of the world as they could into one book. It too hasn't really introduced anything that reveals &quot;new truths&quot;, or alters concepts. <br /> <br /> M20 is going to be our first time I think we see what happens when a developer has gone back and basically re-written the core book from the ground up, but still takes everything that made the fat splat what it was and sort of re-presents it all at once. I get the feeling that Phil didn't lift a single word from previous editions, but rather took what was the &quot;truth&quot; of them to build 20th Anniversary Edition for all fans of Mage: the Ascension.<br /> <br /> Wraith:20, IMO, may be one of the first opportunities for one of the X20 books to really have to look at itself and ask &quot;do I keep the mechanics/game as it was, or do I alter it to appeal to a larger audience?&quot; I suspect we will see a similar treatment to Wraith:20 as we'll have seen from the previous 3, but maybe we'll get some &quot;Storyteller options&quot;, or new light cast in some ways that make it more... digestible to a greater audience. Then again, the X20 lines are about honoring the fans of the original games, not necessarily drawing new players in. It was also the only line to have an official end in the story, so we'll see how that's handled too...<br /> <br /> C:20 will be influenced by the previous 4, and by the developer chosen for the project--if the developer just wants to re-hash the old book, then there won't be much change, but if they really take to it and use this to create something that it never had a chance to become, then we may see something that has learned from the last 10+ years of games and the emergence of the mainstream Modern Fantasy that it was the beginning of as well. The parts of T:tL that were also in C:tD but under-represented may be highlighted IF they would enhance the game, and it'll be interesting to see if Cantrip cards make a return as well (even as an optional rule, or stretch-goal on DriveThruCards.)<br /> <br /> Will highlighting old areas of the C:tD game that weren't well illuminated make the game more fun for old players and introduce and be fun for new players? I guess we'll just have to see what the direction Rich and the new author/developer decide to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T08:09:39-08:00","id":81596,"title":"","content":"I'm really looking forward to seeing what they decide to do with Wraith for its 20th anniversary edition. It historically had lower sales than Changeling, which is why it was canceled while Changeling and serval other games were moved to Arthaus. The sorts of changes that are made to Wraith will give us an idea of were the smaller games might fall on the nostalgia vs. change spectrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}